    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "fc18d941e889de5be7e4310d5f765ae8",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"electron-anomalous-magnetic-moment\">Electron anomalous magnetic moment</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse all notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_bubble.py\">Unequal-mass bubble</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_phi4.py\">Two-loop \u03c6\u2074</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate the QED vertex and extract its Pauli form factor, reproducing\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QED/OneLoop/El-GaEl\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc's one-loop g\u22122 example</a>.\nBoth electrons are on shell, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2=p'^2=m^2||)</marimo-tex>, while the photon probes a\nspacelike momentum transfer <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(q=p-p'||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t=q^2&lt;0||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Between the external spinors the vertex has the form\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((F_1+F_2)\\gamma^\\mu-F_2(p+p')^\\mu/(2m)||)</marimo-tex>.\nShared spin sums close the Dirac traces; a two-by-two Symbolica system\nextracts the coefficient of <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((p+p')^\\mu/(2m)||)</marimo-tex>.\nWe project at generic <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t||)</marimo-tex> and take <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t\\to0||)</marimo-tex> only after integration because\nthose two projectors become degenerate at zero momentum transfer.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">All generator weights are retained. Normalizing to the generated tree\nvertex fixes the coupling and external-fermion phase convention. The\ncommon loop measure is <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(i/(16\\pi^2)||)</marimo-tex> in the OneLOop normalization.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
